      Path: 
    TutorialSteps:
    - header: 
      message: 1/8 <br><br> In this game, you control the order in which mages take
        their predetermined actions  to complete an objective. <br><br> Click the
        box to dismiss.
      uiElement: 5
    - header: 
      message: 2/8 <br><br> This is the Turn Order Bar. Each portrait in it represents
        a mage in the field. You can drag the portraits to determine the order in
        which mages cast their spells. <br><br> Click the box to dismiss.
      uiElement: 7
    - header: 
      message: 3/8 <br><br> The left-most mage will go first and the right-most mage
        will go last. <br><br> Click the box to dismiss.
      uiElement: 7
    - header: 
      message: 4/8 <br><br> In this level, you control the Vetruni mages. They fire
        wind projectiles that push the target they hit.  <br> <br>Click the box to
        dismiss.
      uiElement: 5
    - header: 
      message: 5/8 <br><br> You can hover over both portraits and mages in the level
        to see a preview of their spell. <br><br> Click the box to dismiss.
      uiElement: 5
    - header: 
      message: 6/8 <br> <br>You can use also left-click to lock and unlock previews
        and right-click to access a mage's information panel. <br><br> Click the
        box to dismiss.
      uiElement: 7
    - header: 
      message: 7/8 <br> <br>This is the level objective. You must fulfill it to pass
        the level. <br> <br>Click the box to dismiss.
      uiElement: 8
    - header: 
      message: 8/8 <br><br> When you are ready, press Play to see whether you created
        the correct order. If your order is wrong, a Restart button will appear.
        <br><br> Click the box to dismiss.
      uiElement: 9
